course: dictionary
lesson: 15444
title: A place word: steelworks
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A steelworks is a factory where steel is made. Steel is made from iron and other materials, and huge furnaces are used to make it.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Mum says the steelworks makes the metal for bridges and cars.» The steelworks makes something, so it must be a place where things are made, a factory.
explain: The word is made from two words: steel and works. Here, works means a factory or place where things are made. A steelworks is a noun, and it is the same word for one or many: one steelworks, two steelworks.
fact: A steelworks is a factory where steel is made.
fact: Steel is made from iron and other materials, using huge furnaces.
fact: In science, steel is made by removing carbon and other impurities from iron.
fact: Towns such as Sheffield, Port Talbot and Pittsburgh were famous for their steelworks.
fact: When a steelworks closes, people can lose their jobs; this is called redundancy.
exercise: «Dad started work at the steelworks last week.» Where did Dad work? | *A factory where steel is made | A school for children | A farm with animals | A bakery
exercise: «The old steelworks is now quiet and empty.» What does old mean in this sentence? | Brand new | *Used in the past, no longer working | Painted in bright colours | Very tall
exercise: «When the steelworks closed, many families faced redundancy.» What does redundancy mean here? | Starting a new school | Getting a pay rise | Moving to a new house | *Losing their jobs
test: «The steelworks uses huge furnaces to make steel from iron.» What is steel made from? | *Iron and other materials | Plastic and glass | Sand and water | Wood and paper
test: «Sheffield was famous for its steelworks.» What kind of town is Sheffield here? | A town with no factories | A mountain camp | A small island | *An industrial town
exam: «In science, steel is made by removing carbon and other impurities from iron.» What is removed from iron to make steel? | Sand | *Carbon and other impurities | Paint | Water
